{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-79330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4y.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y={e}^{-4x}$\n- $y={e}^{4x}$\n- $y=4{e}^{x}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-79330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{-4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-4{e}^{-4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ -4{e}^{-4x} & \\overset{?}{=}4{e}^{-4x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 8{e}^{-4x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y={e}^{-4x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y={e}^{4x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{4x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{4x} & =4{e}^{4x}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y={e}^{4x}$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=4{e}^{x},$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{x}.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4y \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}4(4{e}^{x}) \\\\ 4{e}^{x} & \\overset{?}{=}16{e}^{x} \\\\ 0 & \\ne 12{e}^{x}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *not true* for all $x.$ Therefore, the function $y=4{e}^{x}$ is *not* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-79330" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ca52bc93660ff3ec41ee8d6300d81e7d44460f4c611f993b95adf8805394af7"} {"question" "q-79330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-79330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-79330" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141092" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.\n$$\n\n Which of the following is a solution to this equation?\n\n- $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141092" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a function $f(x)$ to be a solution to a differential equation, it must satisfy the equation for all values of $x$ in the equation's domain.\n\nWe check each proposed solution by differentiating and substituting it into the original equation. \n\n- Differentiating $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\n- Differentiating $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Substituting into the original equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-y\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & \\overset{?}{=}-(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis statement is *true*. Therefore, the function $y=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ *is* a solution to our differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141092" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ca52bc93660ff3ec41ee8d6300d81e7d44460f4c611f993b95adf8805394af7"} {"question" "q-141092" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141092" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141092" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4y}{x},\\,y(-1)=-1.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=A{x}^{4}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $y=A{x}^{4}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(-1)=-1.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(-1)=-1$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =A{x}^{4} \\\\ -1 & =A(-1)^{4} \\\\ -1 & =A(1) \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=(-1){x}^{4}=-{x}^{4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141107" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ca52bc93660ff3ec41ee8d6300d81e7d44460f4c611f993b95adf8805394af7"} {"question" "q-141107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141107" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{2},\\,y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{1}{A+x}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $y=\\frac{1}{A+x}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(0)=\\frac{1}{2}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{A+x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{A+0} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{1}{A} \\\\ A & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2+x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ca52bc93660ff3ec41ee8d6300d81e7d44460f4c611f993b95adf8805394af7"} {"question" "q-141116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-141116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-352660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{4y}{x},\\,y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nYou're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}}$ is the solution to this initial value problem. What is the value of the constant $A?$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-352660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We're given that $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}}$ is the solution to the initial value problem. Therefore, it must satisfy the differential equation *and* the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nSubstituting the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{3}{4}$ into our solution and solving for $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{A}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{A}{{2}^{4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{A}{16} \\\\ A & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-352660" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3ca52bc93660ff3ec41ee8d6300d81e7d44460f4c611f993b95adf8805394af7"} {"question" "q-352660" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"} {"question" "q-352660" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14039862/state.json" "file_sha256" "fab06c586b529823fdfe6c4cf06029d95279728ea2fd9f2425b7b84f2c86709e"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1387 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
